    "body": "With a dialog in a dialog, I think that nothing prevents `dialog.firstChild.requestFullscreen()` while this \"blocked by a modal dialog\" definition holds true for the outermost dialog, which would make it such that the innermost dialog fullscreen element becomes the topmost dialog element in document's top layer.\r\n\r\nThe vague \"may provide a user interface\" that applies when blocked by a modal dialog makes me unsure if this is a problem. I can't immediately find a place where Blink does something like this. @upsuper, does this map onto something in Gecko?",
